/* Finnish — and no longer empty, which is the whole point of this note.

   It WAS empty, deliberately, while Finnish was the development language: a key
   with no entry renders as itself, the keys are the Finnish source strings, and
   an identity table would have been a second copy of every string to keep in
   step with the first.

   That stopped being true on 30 Aug 2026, when English became the default. The
   fallback for a missing key is the DEVELOPMENT language, not the key — so a
   Finnish phone looked here, found nothing, fell through to en.lproj and got
   English. The app spoke the wrong language to the one person it was built for,
   which is exactly what the old comment in project.yml warned about, in the
   other direction.

   So every key maps to itself. It is generated from the keys of
   en.lproj/Localizable.strings rather than typed, and scripts/localisation-check.mjs
   fails if the two tables stop matching. Do not hand-edit one without the other.

   189 entries, generated 30 Aug 2026. */

